    "Native normalization records only actual removed pipe-escape events and leading trim; sparse storage grows geometrically",
    "Only owned header/body rows with source positions collect metadata; speculative/delimiter checks skip it",
    "Temporary/discarded cell and final node teardown free metadata through the native allocator",
    "Read-only local non-upstream C accessors expose bounded start/end mapping and borrowed sparse events",
    "Swift verifies normalized bytes against the physical line in one linear sparse-event walk before applying coordinates",
    "Recursive inline scopes inherit the exact outer fragment map; native pointers stay within balanced callbacks",
    "Body rows use their own physical line origin and end; supported custom-inline children are admitted",
    "No source rewriting or second Markdown grammar; native patch records reverse to exact original upstream hashes"
